{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014mMhFGDgAyBnC5E1xuPKMN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (plain-text, local Git, no syncing).\n\n- **Purpose** â€” A GTD-style task/project manager whose source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`). Tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done / Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored.\n\n- **What it ships (core app)** â€” `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) offers the same operations and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Reliability** â€” A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises all endpoints and state transitions (with all model calls stubbed), and writes dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **The R&D \"control surface\" (the bulk of recent work)** â€” A layered subsystem turning each project into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven R&D (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill chain). It has evolved through four merged versions:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated AI summaries, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, deliverable pin/declare, and an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the one allowed native dep, `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, stacking window manager, in-place summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (port-guarded â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (merged 2026-06-13, incl. v4.1 clean rebuild) â€” Paradigm-2 lane tiles with status lights â†’ inline expanding panels (summary over a resizable xterm.js terminal), a skill-auto-loads-once/greets-once seed that fixes the repeating-prompt bug, a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, project cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-promote-to-lane, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Design constraint** â€” Python stdlib only, with one deliberate exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only); `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import. Everything stays human-readable and CLI-accessible â€” no database, no binary/compiled assets."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a11b11a0-7cb7-417c-9e2f-3832d1b060b6","uuid":"b3c90702-9a97-40a4-8f64-275fa9aea997","request_id":"req_011Cc2LM9UE4irbmGvFvDCwW"}
